node_modules/
dist/
# The demo database and the press log — made on each computer by `npm run demo`.
data/
*.log
.env
.DS_Store

# Scratch data directories the suites create beside themselves when run in
# place — which is what CI does, and what anyone without the original
# sandbox does. They are per-run and must never be offered up as changes.
#
# Every directory, not a prefix list: the suites use twenty different ones
# (r54a-, r57-, tg38-, walk-, d52-, x53-, smoke-, f51- …) and `qa/r5*-*/`
# caught seven of them. qa/ holds only files, so any directory appearing
# there is scratch by definition — including whatever the next suite invents.
qa/*/

# The screenshots the suites take to look at what they are testing. Per-run
# evidence, the same as the scratch directories above — regenerated on every
# gate and never worth a diff.
qa/*.png
# …and the ones a suite drops in the repo root when it is run from there.
# Same thing, different working directory.
/*.png

# The deployment's own secrets and pm2 logs — server-side, never committed.
.env.production
logs/

# The screenshots the board shows ARE kept: design-overview/screens/*.png
!design-overview/screens/*.png

# Editor/agent scratch: a local dev launch config, not the project.
.claude/
